WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.000
Cherry blossom petals fall every spring. The team turned them into the active layer of a device that makes electricity.

2
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.960
Every time the petal layer touches another layer and separates, a signal appears without external power.

3
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.960
Calculations and surface probe measurements showed how the petal exchanges charge.

4
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.460
The petal device produced 613 volts and lit 180 LEDs.

5
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:34.080
It held up over twenty two thousand five hundred cycles and worked from minus 4 to 100 degrees Celsius.

6
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:42.560
Machine learning told single taps from double taps with 94.74 percent accuracy. A touch sensor made of petals.
